    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0538" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg454"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-12-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 17, 1902</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1002.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your telegraphic instructions of the 12th instant, and to inclose a copy of
                    the note which I thereupon addressed to His Majesty’s secretary of state for
                    foreign affairs, setting forth the position assumed by our Government with
                    respect to the “pacific” blockade proposed by Germany.</p>
                <p>I have not yet received a reply to this note, but I have ascertained that this
                    Government declined some time ago to assent to Germany proposal for a “pacific”
                    blockade on the ground that they have always maintained a blockade <hi
                        rendition="#italic">jure gentium</hi> to be the only form of blockade
                    admissible.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d431-a1.xml" xpointer="d431-a1"/>
            </div>
